From: Panurus maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 6/10] toolbox: absorb h, z3 and z4 into the Fiat-Shamir transcript

Three prover messages of the toolbox protocol in src/lin-proofs.c were not
bound by the challenges that are meant to bind them
(lazer-crypto/lazer#28):

- h was never hashed: mu, which combines the quadratic equations
  (lnp_quad_many_*), and the final challenge were derived from the hash
  after tg, so a prover could solve for h after seeing mu and make every
  evaluation and quadratic equation hold in combination;
- z3 and z4 were never hashed: the challenges V3/V4 that compress their
  256 linear equations each were derived from hash0, before z3/z4 exist;
- V3/V4 were derived before tg, while the other accumulators feeding h use
  the hash after it, so g could be chosen to cancel an error in the z3/z4
  equations.

h is now absorbed before lnp_quad_many_prove/_verify, z3 and z4 right after
they are computed (prover) or norm-checked (verifier), and V3/V4 are drawn
from the hash after tg. The JL matrices R, R' stay derived from cseed, the
hash before z3/z4, from which the prover computes them. Each round absorbs
the proof's own encoding of the message; coder_grandom3_nbits sizes the
buffer for z3/z4 exactly.

Ported from the fix proposed in the issue thread (and the reporters' fork),
which targets src/lnp-tbox.c: lin_prover_prove and lin_verifier_verify run
the toolbox copy in src/lin-proofs.c, so the fix is applied there, in the
prover and in the verifier. It changes the transcript: proofs made before
and after do not verify against each other. Proof sizes do not change.

Panurus-local patch, applied by `make lazer-install` (lazer.mk).

